  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows early negative signals.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes by applying a 10-15% dampening factor to the immediate next period.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is consistently above true outcome over 5+ days, reduce by 2-3% per day until convergence.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive (sentiment = 0) to avoid underestimating rebounds.",
    "For long-term horizons (>10 days), add a 1-2% upward bias to counteract persistent downward drift in true outcomes.",
    "When sentiment shifts from negative to positive, increase forecast volatility by 10% to capture potential rebound momentum."
  ]
}
